/*!
 * \qmlmodule seal 1.0
 * \title seal QML reference
 * \brief Describe the shared controls in the seal application.
 *
 * Author: \l {https://github.com/openai}{OpenAI Codex}.
 *
 * The QML layer presents application state and sends user actions to C++ view models.
 * Shared controls use the colors, spacing, and motion settings in Theme.qml.
 *
 * \section1 Use a shared action button
 *
 * Use TintedButton for actions in the application workspace. Connect its inherited
 * clicked signal to the view model that owns the action.
 *
 * \qml
 * import QtQuick
 * import seal
 *
 * TintedButton {
 *     text: qsTr("Refresh")
 *     onClicked: workspace.refresh()
 * }
 * \endqml
 *
 * The example assumes that the surrounding view supplies workspace. See the
 * \l {https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qml-qtquick-controls-button.html}{Qt Button reference}
 * for inherited signals and properties.
 *
 * This reference includes all components in qml/. Member comments describe component
 * contracts; inherited Qt API remains in the Qt reference.
 */
